scanner as errors, so a clean run means every call was handled).

Response shapes follow the AWS CLI's bundled service models; see
tests/test_api_models.py, which checks the scanner's field assumptions against
those models independently of this fake.

Environment hooks for tests:
  FAKE_AWS_LOG=path          append "service op" for every call
  FAKE_AWS_ACCOUNT=id        account returned by sts get-caller-identity
  FAKE_AWS_PARTITION=p       ARN partition (default aws)
  FAKE_AWS_FAIL=svc:op,...   make these calls fail (AccessDenied)
  FAKE_AWS_NO_METRICS=a,b    CloudWatch metric names that return no datapoints
  FAKE_AWS_CO_STATUS=Active  Compute Optimizer enrollment status (default Inactive)
  FAKE_AWS_OVERRIDE=json     {"service op": response} to replace canned responses
"""
